acceptance_criteria: "Typed commands cover composite splits, linked devices, automatic entity-ID previews, and entity-ID settings read/update; Write operations fail locally in read-only mode before WebSocket connection; All global output formats, recursive help, docs, schemas, package behavior, live compatibility, and 100/100/100/100 coverage pass"
definition_of_ready: Official Core 2026.8.1 source and tests inspected; all-status PM and GitHub duplicate searches completed; live Core version recorded without private payloads.
goal: agent-native-home-assistant-operations
objective: current-registry-topology-parity
value: Agents can understand device migration and identity topology without raw WebSocket payload knowledge.
impact: Reduces unsafe device targeting and makes Home Assistant 2026.8 entity naming policy inspectable and automatable.
outcome: Production-ready typed registry intelligence with safe mutation boundaries and backward-compatible failure semantics.
why_now: These contracts shipped in the current Core 2026.8.1 release and are absent from the CLI while the local 2026.7.4 instance provides a real compatibility boundary.
